to infected hosts.

242
00:38:38,836 --> 00:38:42,101
The Krippin Virus is...

243
00:38:42,273 --> 00:38:44,264
...elegant.

244
00:38:49,313 --> 00:38:52,441
<i>Just fishing in the dark, son.</i>

245
00:38:55,386 --> 00:38:59,322
Mm. A behavioral note, um:

246
00:39:00,324 --> 00:39:04,818
An infected male
exposed himself to sunlight today.

247
00:39:06,464 --> 00:39:09,797
Now, it's possible
decreased brain function...

248
00:39:09,967 --> 00:39:15,064
...or the growing scarcity of food
is causing them to...

249
00:39:16,240 --> 00:39:20,176
...ignore their basic survival instincts.

250
00:39:22,913 --> 00:39:26,542
Social de-evolution appears complete.

251
00:39:27,051 --> 00:39:31,988
Typical human behavior
is now entirely absent.

252
00:39:38,863 --> 00:39:40,353
Why are we stopping?

253
00:39:44,802 --> 00:39:46,861
The street's closed, folks. We hoof it.

254
00:39:47,037 --> 00:39:50,302
- We got less than 1 0 minutes.
- Baby, give me the dog.

255
00:39:53,944 --> 00:39:55,912
- Come on, baby. Let's go. Let's go.
- Daddy!

256
00:39:56,080 --> 00:39:58,412
It's all right. It's all right. Come on.

257
00:39:58,883 --> 00:40:02,250
Keep the colonel and his family
between us and don't let anyone stop you.

258
00:40:02,420 --> 00:40:03,819
Mommy, they have guns!

259
00:40:03,988 --> 00:40:05,979
It's okay. They're in the Army like Daddy.

260
00:40:06,157 --> 00:40:08,250
<i>Unless you have clearance...</i>

261
00:40:08,426 --> 00:40:11,827
<i>...you cannot pass the checkpoint.
Please return to your homes.</i>

262
00:40:11,996 --> 00:40:15,397
Make a hole, make a hole!
Coming through!

263
00:40:21,005 --> 00:40:23,030
Coming through!

264
00:40:54,572 --> 00:40:58,030
<i>Unless you have clearance,
you cannot pass the checkpoint.</i>

265
00:40:58,209 --> 00:41:00,268
<i>Please return to your homes.</i>

266
00:41:06,050 --> 00:41:08,314
You're clear. Move ahead.

267
00:41:08,752 --> 00:41:09,776
You're clear.

268
00:41:10,221 --> 00:41:12,519
All right, that's it, move up.

269
00:41:13,357 --> 00:41:15,086
All right, step up.

270
00:41:15,559 --> 00:41:17,823
You're clear. Next. Let's go.

271
00:41:19,063 --> 00:41:20,496
No good.

272
00:41:20,664 --> 00:41:23,690
<i>Military quarantine is about to begin.</i>

273
00:41:25,236 --> 00:41:26,794
Come on, step back.

274
00:41:26,971 --> 00:41:29,804
<i>- Military quarantine is about to begin.
- Look, look, look.</i>

275
00:41:29,974 --> 00:41:31,908
- I'm not infected.
- Clear. Good, go on.

276
00:41:32,076 --> 00:41:33,202
I'm not infected.

277
00:41:33,410 --> 00:41:34,809
Please! Please!

278
00:41:34,979 --> 00:41:38,710
- Please take my baby. Take my baby, please.
- You're gonna have to move back.

279
00:41:40,784 --> 00:41:42,251
- No good.
- Follow me, ma'am.

280
00:41:42,419 --> 00:41:45,752
What? No! Robert! Robert!

281
00:41:45,923 --> 00:41:48,118
Get your hands off my wife.
Get your hands off.

282
00:41:48,292 --> 00:41:50,658
- Mommy!
- Stand down.

283
00:41:50,828 --> 00:41:51,852
Lieutenant--

284
00:41:52,029 --> 00:41:54,691
- Mommy!
- Scan her again. Get your hands off of her!

285
00:41:54,865 --> 00:41:56,332
Get your hands off of my wife.

286
00:41:56,500 --> 00:41:58,832
- Stand down!
- Scan her again. Stand down!

287
00:41:59,003 --> 00:42:01,597
Stand down, soldier! Stand down!

288
00:42:01,772 --> 00:42:05,367
I am Lieutenant Colonel Robert Neville.
I am ordering you to scan her again.

289
00:42:05,543 --> 00:42:07,238
Scan her again!

290
00:42:10,781 --> 00:42:12,840
All right, scan her again.

291
00:42:15,853 --> 00:42:18,651
- It's clear.
- It's clear. Move through.

292
00:42:21,025 --> 00:42:22,185
Who's next? Come on.

293
00:42:22,359 --> 00:42:25,260
Take my baby with you!
Please! Please!

294
00:42:25,429 --> 00:42:28,626
- Mommy!
- Please take my baby. Please!

295
00:42:30,067 --> 00:42:33,833
Daddy, why can't the little girl come too?

296
00:42:34,371 --> 00:42:36,566
<i>Stay away from the shoreline.</i>

297
00:42:36,740 --> 00:42:38,401
How long?

298
00:42:38,909 --> 00:42:40,843
Five minutes. We'll make it.

299
00:42:41,011 --> 00:42:44,174
This is Ranger 621, we're on site.

300
00:42:44,748 --> 00:42:47,911
<i>Military quarantine is about to begin.</i>

301
00:42:59,997 --> 00:43:04,991
I won't take my eyes off them, colonel.
You got my word on it.

302
00:43:09,907 --> 00:43:11,499
Give me a kiss.

303
00:43:21,986 --> 00:43:24,648
<i>I love you. I love you.</i>

304
00:43:25,356 --> 00:43:28,223
Dear Lord, please watch over Robert...

305
00:43:28,392 --> 00:43:30,724
...and keep him strong
through the struggles ahead.

306
00:43:30,894 --> 00:43:34,921
Lord, please just bring him home safely.
Amen.

307
00:43:36,467 --> 00:43:38,935
Daddy's gonna make the monsters
go away, baby, okay?

308
00:43:39,103 --> 00:43:41,401
Sam, you protect Daddy.

309
00:43:41,572 --> 00:43:45,531
- No, baby, I can't. Daddy can't take a dog.
- Sir, we gotta go!

310
00:43:48,278 --> 00:43:51,645
Daddy, look, it's a butterfly.

311
00:43:52,282 --> 00:43:54,546
<i>It's a butterfly.</i>

312
00:43:57,054 --> 00:43:59,113
All right, come on, let's go!

313
00:44:45,484 --> 00:44:47,008
How'd you sleep?

314
00:44:47,186 --> 00:44:50,314
<i>Dr. Neville will be taking a closer look
at the ongoing mutations...</i>

315
00:44:50,489 --> 00:44:55,392
<i>...of Dr. Alice Krippin's once-hailed
miracle cure for cancer.</i>

316
00:44:55,561 --> 00:44:59,691
<i>So far, almost 5000 patients
treated with her retrofitted virus...</i>

317
00:44:59,865 --> 00:45:03,699
<i>...have begun exhibiting symptoms
resembling the early onset of rabies.</i>

318
00:45:03,869 --> 00:45:06,667
<i>Twenty-five patients have already died.</i>

319
00:45:06,839 --> 00:45:11,037
<i>Dr. Neville has ordered local hospitals
to stockpile antiviral drugs...</i>

320
00:45:11,210 --> 00:45:14,145
<i>...and to begin
preliminary quarantine protocols.</i>

321
00:45:14,313 --> 00:45:15,871
It's my birthday.

322
00:45:16,048 --> 00:45:19,415
<i>We are fully confident Dr. Neville
can see us through these--</i>

323
00:45:19,585 --> 00:45:21,280
You gonna sing?

324
00:45:22,221 --> 00:45:24,655
<i>My name is Robert Neville.</i>

325
00:45:25,190 --> 00:45:28,387
<i>I am a survivor living in New York City.</i>

326
00:45:30,396 --> 00:45:34,127
<i>I am broadcasting on all AM frequencies.</i>

327
00:45:34,767 --> 00:45:38,396
<i>I will be at the South Street Seaport
every day at midday...</i>

328
00:45:38,570 --> 00:45:41,403
<i>...when the sun is highest in the sky.</i>

329
00:45:42,574 --> 00:45:47,637
<i>If you are out there,
if anyone is out there...</i>

330
00:45:47,813 --> 00:45:52,011
<i>I can provide food. I can provide shelter.</i>

331
00:45:52,184 --> 00:45:54,914
<i>I can provide security.</i>

332
00:45:55,087 --> 00:45:58,579
<i>If there's anybody out there, anybody...</i>

333
00:46:00,926 --> 00:46:02,723
<i>Please.</i>

334
00:46:03,328 --> 00:46:05,319
<i>You are not alone.</i>

335
00:46:06,331 --> 00:46:07,923
Listen, uh...

336
00:46:08,100 --> 00:46:11,467
...if you're planning a party or something,
just tell me now.

337
00:46:11,770 --> 00:46:14,534
Okay? Because you know
I don't like surprises.

338
00:46:14,706 --> 00:46:18,301
And I swear I'll act surprised. Okay?

339
00:46:48,307 --> 00:46:50,070
Hey! Hey!

340
00:47:03,188 --> 00:47:06,282
What the hell
are you doing out here, Fred?!

341
00:47:08,861 --> 00:47:11,989
What the--? What the hell are you--?
No!

342
00:47:12,464 --> 00:47:14,864
No! No!

343
00:47:17,069 --> 00:47:18,400
No.

344
00:47:18,570 --> 00:47:21,437
What the hell
are you doing out here, Fred?!

345
00:47:21,807 --> 00:47:24,071
How did you get out here?!

346
00:47:24,173 --> 00:47:27,336
Fred, if you're real,
you better tell me right now!

347
00:47:27,509 --> 00:47:30,945
If you're real,
you better tell me right now!

348
00:47:43,926 --> 00:47:46,053
Damn it, Fred!

349
00:47:46,595 --> 00:47:48,586
Damn it!

350
00:49:49,084 --> 00:49:52,485
I'm all right. I'm all right, I'm all right.

351
00:50:18,313 --> 00:50:21,180
I'm all right. I'm all right. I'm all right.

352
00:50:46,541 --> 00:50:49,169
Baby. I'm okay.

353
00:50:50,112 --> 00:50:53,275
I'm okay. I'm okay.

354
00:52:10,892 --> 00:52:12,655
Let's go.

355
00:52:12,828 --> 00:52:15,763
Eh, eh! Come on. Sam, come on.

356
00:52:28,210 --> 00:52:29,302
Let's go! Sam!

357
00:52:39,588 --> 00:52:41,351
No! No! Let's go!

358
00:52:41,523 --> 00:52:44,253
We gotta go home, Sam. Let's go!

359
00:53:13,054 --> 00:53:14,487
Sam!

360
00:53:20,896 --> 00:53:22,761
No!

361
00:53:46,455 --> 00:53:48,855
Sam? Sam?

362
00:53:51,626 --> 00:53:52,991
It's okay.

363
00:53:53,161 --> 00:53:56,221
You're all right. Okay. It's okay.

364
00:53:56,398 --> 00:53:58,889
You're all right. You're all right.

365
00:53:59,301 --> 00:54:02,031
Samantha? Samantha, look at me, girl.

366
00:54:02,204 --> 00:54:06,436
Hey. You're okay.
You're okay. Samantha.

367
00:54:06,608 --> 00:54:09,771
We just gotta get you home.
Gotta get you-- Gotta take you home.

368
00:54:09,945 --> 00:54:12,505
Let me take you home.
All right, come here.

369
00:54:12,681 --> 00:54:15,149
Come here. Come here. Come here.

370
00:54:50,051 --> 00:54:51,609
Come on. Come here. Come here.

371
00:54:51,887 --> 00:54:54,219
I got you. I got you.

372
00:55:01,229 --> 00:55:02,958
It's okay.

373
00:55:03,865 --> 00:55:05,594
You're okay.

374
00:55:13,675 --> 00:55:15,404
<i>Don't worry</i>

375
00:55:17,612 --> 00:55:19,739
<i>About a thing</i>

376
00:55:20,782 --> 00:55:25,947
<i>'Cause every little thing
Is gonna be all right</i>

377
00:55:29,424 --> 00:55:35,056
<i>Don't worry
About a thing</i>

378
00:55:39,868 --> 00:55:42,302
<i>Rise up this morning</i>

379
00:55:43,939 --> 00:55:46,533
<i>Smiled with the rising sun</i>

380
00:55:52,847 --> 00:55:54,872
<i>Three little birds</i>

381
00:58:58,099 --> 00:59:00,533
I promised my friend...

382
00:59:02,170 --> 00:59:07,335
...that I would say hello to you today.

383
00:59:12,013 --> 00:59:13,742
Hello.

384
00:59:21,489 --> 00:59:23,184
Hello.

385
00:59:33,668 --> 00:59:36,466
Please say hello to me.

386
00:59:43,344 --> 00:59:46,108
Please say hello to me.

387
01:01:06,594 --> 01:01:08,152
Die!

388
01:01:08,463 --> 01:01:09,555
Die!

389
01:01:23,578 --> 01:01:25,307
Die!

390
01:03:05,313 --> 01:03:08,714
Come on! Stay with me!

391
01:03:10,251 --> 01:03:12,811
Where do you live?

392
01:03:14,655 --> 01:03:16,520
Hey.

393
01:03:16,991 --> 01:03:18,515
Hey!

394
01:03:18,693 --> 01:03:20,820
Stay with me.

395
01:03:21,729 --> 01:03:23,993
Where do you live?

396
01:03:26,968 --> 01:03:29,493
Where do you live?

397
01:03:30,271 --> 01:03:31,499
Uh...

398
01:03:31,672 --> 01:03:35,870
1 1 Washington Square.

399
01:03:36,411 --> 01:03:39,141
They don't know where I live.

400
01:03:40,048 --> 01:03:43,506
Don't-- Don't let them track us.

401
01:03:43,951 --> 01:03:46,476
You gotta stay out till dawn.

402
01:04:50,351 --> 01:04:51,340
No!

403
01:04:52,920 --> 01:04:54,854
<i>Donkey?</i>

404
01:04:55,823 --> 01:04:56,915
<i>What are you doing?</i>

405
01:04:57,091 --> 01:05:00,424
<i>I would think of all people you would
recognize a wall when you see one.</i>

406
01:05:00,595 --> 01:05:05,362
<i>Well, yeah. But the wall's supposed to go
around my swamp, not through it.</i>

407
01:05:05,533 --> 01:05:08,502
<i>It is. Around your half, see?
That's your half, this is my half.</i>

408
01:05:08,669 --> 01:05:12,230
<i>- Oh, your half? Hm.
- Yes, my half.</i>

409
01:05:12,406 --> 01:05:16,035
<i>I helped rescue the princess. I did
half the work. I get half the booty.</i>

410
01:05:16,210 --> 01:05:19,577
<i>Now hand me that big old rock,
the one that looks like your head.</i>

411
01:05:19,747 --> 01:05:21,874
<i>- Back off!
- No, you back off.</i>

412
01:05:22,049 --> 01:05:24,108
<i>- This is my swamp!
- Our swamp.</i>

413
01:05:26,954 --> 01:05:29,752
<i>- Smelly ogre.
- Fine!</i>

414
01:05:30,458 --> 01:05:32,187
<i>Come back,
I'm not through with you!</i>

415
01:05:32,360 --> 01:05:33,850
<i>Well, I'm through with you.</i>

416
01:05:34,028 --> 01:05:37,122
<i>You know, with you it's always "me, me, me."</i>

417
01:05:37,298 --> 01:05:42,361
<i>Well, guess what, now it's my turn.
So you just shut up and pay attention!</i>

418
01:05:42,537 --> 01:05:46,701
<i>You are mean to me! You insult me and
you don't appreciate anything that I do.</i>

419
01:05:46,874 --> 01:05:49,274
<i>You're always pushing me around
or pushing me away.</i>

420
01:05:49,443 --> 01:05:53,812
<i>Oh, yeah? Well, if I treated you so bad,
how come you came back?</i>

421
01:05:53,981 --> 01:05:57,144
<i>Because that's what friends do!
They forgive each other!</i>

422
01:05:57,518 --> 01:05:59,213
<i>Oh, yeah.</i>

423
01:05:59,387 --> 01:06:01,719
<i>You're right, Donkey. I forgive you...</i>

424
01:06:01,889 --> 01:06:03,356
<i>...for stabbing me in the back!</i>

425
01:06:06,727 --> 01:06:10,219
<i>You're so wrapped up in layers,
you're afraid of your own feelings.</i>

426
01:06:10,398 --> 01:06:11,558
<i>- Go away.
- See?</i>

427
01:06:11,732 --> 01:06:13,859
<i>Doing it again,
just like you did to Fiona...</i>

428
01:06:14,035 --> 01:06:16,230
<i>...and all she did was like you,
maybe love you.</i>

429
01:06:16,404 --> 01:06:20,864
<i>Love me? She said I was ugly,
a hideous creature.</i>

430
01:06:21,042 --> 01:06:22,669
<i>I heard the two of you talking.</i>

431
01:06:22,843 --> 01:06:27,678
<i>She wasn't talking about you,
she was talking about somebody else.</i>

432
01:06:36,724 --> 01:06:39,192
I'm afraid the eggs are powdered.

433
01:06:39,360 --> 01:06:41,385
Obviously you know that.

434
01:06:42,263 --> 01:06:43,457
They're yours.

435
01:06:43,631 --> 01:06:48,625
But I did find bacon, which is about
the most fantastic thing in history.

436
01:06:48,803 --> 01:06:52,603
And some antibiotics in the bathroom.

437
01:06:52,773 --> 01:06:55,139
I put by your plate,
because your leg is okay...

438
01:06:55,309 --> 01:06:59,507
...but it won't be for very long
if you don't start a course soon.

439
01:07:00,815 --> 01:07:02,612
Who are you?

440
01:07:04,085 --> 01:07:06,645
I'm Anna and that's Ethan.

441
01:07:13,728 --> 01:07:15,855
Don't let it get cold.

442
01:07:28,776 --> 01:07:31,540
It's okay. Go on.

443
01:07:56,704 --> 01:08:00,800
We came from Maryland.
We heard your message on the radio.

444
01:08:01,509 --> 01:08:04,569
We were at the pier at noon.
We waited all day.

445
01:08:06,547 --> 01:08:09,015
We're going to Vermont.

446
01:08:09,684 --> 01:08:12,346
To the survivors' colony.

447
01:08:12,920 --> 01:08:14,512
What?

448
01:08:15,456 --> 01:08:19,085
In Bethel. It's a safe zone.

449
01:08:19,260 --> 01:08:21,728
There's no survivors' colony,
there's no safe zones.

450
01:08:21,896 --> 01:08:23,761
Nothing happened
the way it was supposed to.

451
01:08:24,098 --> 01:08:25,998
Nothing worked
the way it was supposed to.

452
01:08:26,167 --> 01:08:30,763
In the mountains. There's a whole colony
of people there who didn't get sick.

453
01:08:30,938 --> 01:08:33,463
The virus couldn't survive the cold.
There's a colony--

454
01:08:33,641 --> 01:08:35,871
Shut up! Shut up!

455
01:08:36,043 --> 01:08:37,476
Everybody's dead.

456
01:08:37,712 --> 01:08:39,771
Everybody is dead.

457
01:08:47,722 --> 01:08:50,816
I just need--
I need a minute. Okay?

458
01:08:52,426 --> 01:08:53,950
<i>Just...</i>

459
01:08:57,865 --> 01:09:00,766
I just-- I was saving that bacon.

460
01:09:02,336 --> 01:09:03,633
I was saving it.

461
01:09:06,474 --> 01:09:08,942
<i>I'm just-- I'm gonna go upstairs.
All right? Just--</i>

462
01:09:09,110 --> 01:09:11,135
I'm gonna go.

463
01:09:29,263 --> 01:09:31,891
Ethan, put the knife down.

464
01:10:06,901 --> 01:10:10,837
<i>- You there! Ogre.
- Aye.</i>

465
01:10:11,005 --> 01:10:13,166
<i>By the order of Lord Farquaad...</i>

466
01:10:13,340 --> 01:10:15,740
<i>...I am authorized
to place you both under arrest...</i>

467
01:10:15,910 --> 01:10:21,712
<i>...and transport you
to a designated resettlement facility.</i>

468
01:10:21,882 --> 01:10:26,251
<i>Oh, really? You and what army?</i>

469
01:10:37,531 --> 01:10:39,192
Can I say something to you?

470
01:10:39,366 --> 01:10:42,358
You was really, really something
back there. Incredible.

471
01:10:42,703 --> 01:10:44,728
Are you talking to...

472
01:10:45,873 --> 01:10:46,897
...me?

473
01:10:48,342 --> 01:10:51,573
Yes, I was talking to you.
You was really great back there.

474
01:10:51,745 --> 01:10:54,976
Those guards, they thought they was
all that. You showed up, and bam!

475
01:10:55,149 --> 01:10:57,413
Tripping over themselves
like babes in the woods.

476
01:10:57,585 --> 01:10:59,610
That really made me
feel good to see that.

477
01:10:59,787 --> 01:11:01,982
That's great. Really.
Man, it's good to be free.

478
01:11:02,456 --> 01:11:06,290
Now, why don't you go celebrate
your freedom with your own friends?

479
01:11:06,460 --> 01:11:07,950
Hm?

480
01:11:08,128 --> 01:11:09,561
But, uh...

481
01:11:09,797 --> 01:11:11,355
...I don't have any friends.

482
01:11:11,532 --> 01:11:14,000
And I'm not going out there by myself.

483
01:11:14,168 --> 01:11:16,796
Wait a minute. I got a great idea.
I'll stick with you!

484
01:11:16,971 --> 01:11:18,734
<i>You a mean, green fighting machine.</i>

485
01:11:18,906 --> 01:11:22,000
<i>Together we'll scare the spit
out of anybody that crosses us.</i>

486
01:11:25,246 --> 01:11:26,508
<i>I like Shrek.</i>

487
01:11:26,680 --> 01:11:29,114
<i>That was really scary.
If you don't mind me saying...</i>

488
01:11:29,283 --> 01:11:32,013
<i>...if that don't work, your breath
will get the job done...</i>

489
01:11:32,186 --> 01:11:36,122
<i>...because you definitely need some
tic tacs, because your breath stinks!</i>

490
01:11:36,724 --> 01:11:40,751
<i>Man, you almost burned the hair
out of my nose. Just like the time...</i>

491
01:11:43,230 --> 01:11:45,858
You're not so good with people anymore,
are you?

492
01:11:51,305 --> 01:11:53,830
Thank you for my leg.

493
01:11:56,343 --> 01:11:58,106
Okay.

494
01:12:01,181 --> 01:12:02,705
Where have you been?

495
01:12:02,950 --> 01:12:06,511
I was on a Red Cross evacuation ship
out of Säo Paulo.

496
01:12:06,687 --> 01:12:09,781
Those boats
weren't meant to be permanent.

497
01:12:09,957 --> 01:12:11,515
No, they weren't.

498
01:12:11,692 --> 01:12:14,684
When the Navy fell apart,
we started docking to take on supplies.

499
01:12:14,862 --> 01:12:18,628
Someone picked it up on shore.
Five of us were immune.

500
01:12:18,799 --> 01:12:20,460
You said five?

501
01:12:21,135 --> 01:12:23,501
The Darkseekers got them.

502
01:12:25,873 --> 01:12:28,501
You are the Robert Neville, aren't you?

503
01:12:37,351 --> 01:12:38,716
It's too late today.

504
01:12:38,886 --> 01:12:42,014
If we leave tomorrow at dawn, we can
make it to Vermont in a straight shot.

505
01:12:42,189 --> 01:12:44,657
- So if you had--
- I'm not leaving.

506
01:12:45,526 --> 01:12:47,858
This is ground zero.

507
01:12:49,296 --> 01:12:51,457
This is my site.

508
01:12:53,100 --> 01:12:55,591
I'm not gonna let this happen.

509
01:12:57,771 --> 01:13:00,069
I can still fix this.

510
01:13:04,878 --> 01:13:06,846
What happened to your leg?

511
01:13:09,350 --> 01:13:13,446
That's my snare.
These are my materials.

512
01:13:13,621 --> 01:13:16,647
The infected didn't do this. They can't.

513
01:13:17,191 --> 01:13:20,490
- How do you know?
- They have no higher brain function.

514
01:13:20,661 --> 01:13:25,928
They don't plan or hate.
They don't love. They can't.

515
01:13:30,571 --> 01:13:32,129
Could they be evolving?

516
01:13:38,545 --> 01:13:40,410
Ethan.

517
01:13:44,051 --> 01:13:46,110
Hey, Ethan.

518
01:13:54,528 --> 01:13:55,654
It's cold.

519
01:14:04,438 --> 01:14:05,462
We gotta go.

520
01:14:08,042 --> 01:14:10,169
- I've been cooking the compounds.
- What?

521
01:14:10,344 --> 01:14:12,778
Ice. I need ice.

522
01:14:21,255 --> 01:14:25,919
- Whoa. You scared me.
- Sorry.

523
01:14:26,093 --> 01:14:27,424
I called down twice.

524
01:14:27,594 --> 01:14:30,256
Oh. Oh, thank you.

525
01:14:34,935 --> 01:14:38,530
It's heavily sedated.
Don't worry, it's safe.

526
01:14:38,706 --> 01:14:41,436
I've never seen one so still.

527
01:14:42,042 --> 01:14:44,738
They're always biting.

528
01:14:48,749 --> 01:14:51,081
You think that can cure her?

529
01:14:51,251 --> 01:14:54,186
Um... No, this will
almost certainly kill it...

530
01:14:54,354 --> 01:14:57,585
...but it's possible by drastically reducing
the body temperature...

531
01:14:57,758 --> 01:15:00,750
...I can increase the compound's
effectiveness.

532
01:15:12,039 --> 01:15:14,337
Did all of them die?

533
01:15:14,575 --> 01:15:16,133
Yes.

534
01:15:19,213 --> 01:15:21,204
My God.

535
01:15:22,049 --> 01:15:25,780
God didn't do this, Anna, we did.

536
01:15:31,125 --> 01:15:33,457
Where can Ethan sleep?

537
01:15:52,146 --> 01:15:54,011
He's heavy.

538
01:16:00,521 --> 01:16:02,318
Can you get that?

539
01:16:34,121 --> 01:16:36,419
She's beautiful.

540
01:16:36,890 --> 01:16:38,790
What's her name?

541
01:16:40,494 --> 01:16:42,394
Marley.

542
01:16:43,664 --> 01:16:47,225
- Her name was Marley.
- It's a beautiful name.

543
01:16:49,136 --> 01:16:53,163
Yeah. We named her after Bob Marley.

544
01:16:53,340 --> 01:16:56,673
- Who?
- Uh, the singer.

545
01:16:57,711 --> 01:16:59,440
Damian?

546
01:17:00,714 --> 01:17:02,739
Uh, his father.

547
01:17:06,019 --> 01:17:08,283
His father.

548
01:17:09,356 --> 01:17:10,482
Nope.

549
01:17:10,657 --> 01:17:12,750
<i>I shot the sheriff</i>

550
01:17:16,063 --> 01:17:19,032
<i>But I didn't shoot the deputy</i>

551
01:17:26,540 --> 01:17:31,568
- Oh, that is unacceptable.
- What?

552
01:17:36,216 --> 01:17:38,707
Best album ever made.

553
01:17:48,061 --> 01:17:51,121
- You don't recognize that?
- Mm-mm.

554
01:17:52,432 --> 01:17:53,660
Wow.

555
01:17:55,836 --> 01:18:01,399
He had this idea,
it was kind of a virologist's idea.

556
01:18:01,575 --> 01:18:06,205
He believed that you could cure
racism and hate. Literally cure it...

557
01:18:06,380 --> 01:18:12,512
...by injecting music and love
into people's lives.

558
01:18:13,353 --> 01:18:17,221
One day, he was scheduled
to perform at a peace rally.

559
01:18:17,391 --> 01:18:21,350
Gunmen came to his house
and shot him down.

560
01:18:23,196 --> 01:18:24,527
Two days later...

561
01:18:25,165 --> 01:18:28,794
...he walked out on that stage and sang.

562
01:18:30,604 --> 01:18:33,004
Somebody asked him why.

563
01:18:34,808 --> 01:18:37,276
He said, "The people...

564
01:18:37,444 --> 01:18:42,507
...who are trying to make this world worse
are not taking a day off.

565
01:18:43,684 --> 01:18:45,675
How can I?"

566
01:18:48,755 --> 01:18:51,588
Light up the darkness.

567
01:19:17,617 --> 01:19:19,847
Come with us, Neville.

568
01:19:20,420 --> 01:19:22,445
To the colony.

569
01:19:26,159 --> 01:19:28,593
There's no colony, Anna.

570
01:19:32,899 --> 01:19:34,423
Everything just fell apart.

571
01:19:34,601 --> 01:19:38,298
- There was no evacuation plan--
- You're wrong. There is a colony.

572
01:19:38,872 --> 01:19:40,897
I know, okay?

573
01:19:42,342 --> 01:19:43,570
How do you know, Anna?

574
01:19:50,083 --> 01:19:51,141
I just know.

575
01:19:53,420 --> 01:19:57,550
How? I said, how do you know?
How could you know?

576
01:19:59,259 --> 01:20:00,590
God told me.

577
01:20:01,094 --> 01:20:03,085
He has a plan.

578
01:20:04,831 --> 01:20:07,425
- God told you?
- Yes.

579
01:20:07,601 --> 01:20:10,331
- The God?
- Yes.

580
01:20:11,905 --> 01:20:14,339
- I know how this sounds.
- It sounds crazy.

581
01:20:14,508 --> 01:20:18,308
But something told me
to turn on the radio.

582
01:20:18,478 --> 01:20:20,105
Something told me to come here.

583
01:20:20,280 --> 01:20:23,078
My voice on the radio
told you to come here, Anna.

584
01:20:23,250 --> 01:20:25,275
You were trying to kill yourself
last night?

585
01:20:25,452 --> 01:20:26,441
Anna.

586
01:20:26,620 --> 01:20:29,783
I got here just in time to save your life.
That's a coincidence?

587
01:20:29,956 --> 01:20:33,585
<i>- Just stop it. Stop it. Stop.
- He must have sent me here for a reason.</i>

588
01:20:34,761 --> 01:20:37,787
Neville, the world is quieter now.

589
01:20:37,964 --> 01:20:40,023
You just have to listen.

590
01:20:40,200 --> 01:20:42,361
If we listen...

591
01:20:43,036 --> 01:20:45,004
...we can hear God's plan.

592
01:20:45,205 --> 01:20:47,230
- God's plan?
- Yeah.

593
01:20:47,407 --> 01:20:49,967
All right. Let me tell you
about your God's plan.

594
01:20:50,143 --> 01:20:53,044
There were 6 billion people on Earth
when the infection hit.

595
01:20:53,213 --> 01:20:57,809
KV had a 90 percent kill rate.
That's 5.4 billion...

596
01:20:57,984 --> 01:21:00,452
...people dead.

597
01:21:00,620 --> 01:21:03,453
Crashed and bled out, dead.

598
01:21:03,623 --> 01:21:05,488
Less than 1 percent immunity.

599
01:21:05,659 --> 01:21:09,459
That left 12 million healthy people
like you, me and Ethan.

600
01:21:09,629 --> 01:21:13,759
The other 588 million...

601
01:21:13,934 --> 01:21:15,925
...turned into your Darkseekers.

602
01:21:16,103 --> 01:21:17,798
And then they got hungry.

603
01:21:17,971 --> 01:21:22,374
And they killed and fed on everybody.

604
01:21:23,543 --> 01:21:25,636
Everybody!

605
01:21:26,346 --> 01:21:31,306
Every single person
that you or I has ever known...

606
01:21:31,485 --> 01:21:33,419
...is dead!

607
01:21:35,755 --> 01:21:37,655
Dead!

608
01:21:38,992 --> 01:21:41,722
There is no God. There is no God.

609
01:21:47,033 --> 01:21:48,864
What is that?

610
01:21:52,205 --> 01:21:55,538
Was it still dark when you
brought us home last night?

611
01:21:55,709 --> 01:21:58,803
You were bleeding.
There was light on the horizon.

612
01:22:00,380 --> 01:22:03,110
Turn the light off. Turn it off.

613
01:22:10,390 --> 01:22:11,823
They followed us home.

614
01:22:11,992 --> 01:22:13,653
Ethan.

615
01:22:59,839 --> 01:23:01,500
Shit.

616
01:23:14,221 --> 01:23:15,848
Anna.

617
01:23:17,390 --> 01:23:19,187
Anna.

618
01:23:23,964 --> 01:23:25,591
Anna!

619
01:23:37,210 --> 01:23:39,144
Anna!

620
01:23:42,549 --> 01:23:44,141
Anna!

621
01:25:30,590 --> 01:25:32,217
Anna?

622
01:25:36,196 --> 01:25:37,925
Anna.

623
01:26:35,789 --> 01:26:37,984
Come on. Come on.

624
01:26:39,025 --> 01:26:40,993
- Are you okay? You all right?
- Yeah.

625
01:26:41,161 --> 01:26:42,685
Are you all right?

626
01:26:43,329 --> 01:26:44,728
- You okay?
- Oh, my God. You're bleeding.

627
01:26:59,112 --> 01:27:01,706
Go to the lab. Downstairs, go!

628
01:27:01,981 --> 01:27:04,779
Get to the lab! To the lab!

629
01:27:14,127 --> 01:27:15,151
Get behind the Plexi.

630
01:27:15,995 --> 01:27:17,656
Oh, my God. Come on.

631
01:27:30,243 --> 01:27:32,006
Come on, it's okay. It's okay.

632
01:27:33,813 --> 01:27:35,576
Oh, my God.

633
01:27:48,061 --> 01:27:50,052
It's working.

634
01:27:54,400 --> 01:27:55,765
Neville...

635
01:27:57,070 --> 01:27:58,867
...it's working.

636
01:28:04,177 --> 01:28:05,974
No! Stop! Stop!

637
01:28:07,280 --> 01:28:09,578
Look, look, look, I can save you.

638
01:28:09,749 --> 01:28:13,207
I can sa-- I can help you.
You are sick and I can help you.

639
01:28:16,322 --> 01:28:18,290
I can-- I can fix this!

640
01:28:18,458 --> 01:28:19,982
I can save everybody!

641
01:28:20,159 --> 01:28:23,390
I can fix everything! It's working.
It's working!

642
01:28:26,633 --> 01:28:28,066
Stop! Stop!

643
01:28:34,207 --> 01:28:37,643
Let me save you! Let me save you!

644
01:28:37,810 --> 01:28:38,799
No, no!

645
01:28:49,622 --> 01:28:50,953
No, no!

646
01:29:20,386 --> 01:29:23,150
<i>Daddy, look, it's a butterfly.</i>

647
01:30:01,594 --> 01:30:03,152
Robert.

648
01:30:04,263 --> 01:30:06,288
What are you doing?

649
01:30:34,193 --> 01:30:35,626
Open the door, please.

650
01:30:37,964 --> 01:30:39,124
What are you doing?

651
01:30:41,034 --> 01:30:42,797
I'm listening.

652
01:31:06,392 --> 01:31:08,451
Shh, shh, shh...

653
01:31:08,995 --> 01:31:10,462
Don't look.

654
01:31:42,261 --> 01:31:44,024
I need to get a syringe.

655
01:33:18,758 --> 01:33:19,986
I'm sorry.

656
01:34:23,489 --> 01:34:25,354
Shh, shh, shh...

657
01:34:40,239 --> 01:34:42,002
<i>My name is Anna Montez.</i>

658
01:34:43,509 --> 01:34:45,534
<i>There are other survivors.</i>

659
01:34:47,613 --> 01:34:51,913
<i>I am traveling with Dr. Robert Neville
and a boy named Ethan.</i>

660
01:34:52,084 --> 01:34:56,987
<i>We're heading north on Route 1 7
to Bethel, Vermont.</i>

661
01:34:57,156 --> 01:35:02,219
<i>Keep your radio on.
Listen for our broadcasts.</i>

662
01:35:02,662 --> 01:35:05,256
<i>You are not alone.</i>

663
01:35:06,098 --> 01:35:08,464
<i>There is hope.</i>

664
01:35:09,669 --> 01:35:11,830
<i>Keep listening.</i>

665
01:35:13,172 --> 01:35:15,003
<i>You are not alone.</i>

